<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sofala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sofala was a port on the coast of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>, an important centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">gold trade</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> and Arab merchants traded there, and the Portuguese later built a fort. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> profiles mention Sofala as a coastal outlet for gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sofala.jpg" alt="Sofala" width="273" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mallet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sofala1683.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
